  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:4655",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C is shown to have a target relationship with Dual specificity protein kinase CLK4 through two distinct pathways. In the first pathway, Oblonganoside C directly targets Caov-4, which in turn is a target of K-252a, a known inhibitor of Dual specificity protein kinase CLK4. This suggests a direct regulatory link between Oblonganoside C and CLK4 through the Caov-4 cell line. In the second pathway, Oblonganoside C is shown to target Tyrosine-protein kinase Fes/Fps, which is also a target of K-252a, and this kinase subsequently targets CLK4. This indicates that Oblonganoside C may influence CLK4 through a different downstream pathway, potentially involving Fes/Fps. Both pathways suggest that Oblonganoside C exerts its effects on CLK4 via a series of intermediate targets, likely through the K-252a-mediated signaling cascade. The evidence supports a complex, multi-step mechanism by which Oblonganoside C may interact with and modulate the activity of Dual specificity protein kinase CLK4.",
